## Summary of the Web Defense Blueprint
To secure a web application against this absolute baseline of threats, development teams utilize three primary architectural pillars:

   1. Strict Input Allowlisting: Never allowing backend frameworks or database engines to process variables dynamically. Every incoming field must match an exact, strictly defined data type schema.
   2. Defensive API Gateways: Restricting internal network infrastructure so that backend payment systems can never accept requests from the web server unless they are accompanied by a valid, time-limited cryptographic token.
   3. Normalized Routing Standards: Ensuring frontend proxies and backend web runtimes use identical, updated HTTP parsing engines to make Request Smuggling mechanically impossible.

